this message is limited to the FTP aspect of the problem.  you're on
your own after that (nice guy, huh?) ...

it may that your site does not allow you to access remote sites using
ftp (file transfer program/protocol).  if not, you have two alternatives:
(a) a local comp.sources.games archive or better yet (b) e-mail.  the
details on these are to be found in the weekly FAQ's.

let's assume you have ftp and Unix.  try:

ftp 130.91.6.8		{should be equivalent to ftp linc.cis.upenn.edu}
login: anonymous
password: guest

cd pub/NH3.0		{sources are here, binaries in sub-directories}
			{the source is packaged somewhat strangely for}
			{your convenience ...}
prompt			{toggle off prompt mode}
mget READ*		{transfer any file that starts with READ}
quit

read the READ* files and follow directions.

you're also on your own if you need to compile the sources.  binaries
are available for the PC, os2, amiga, atari, and macintosh.  VMS and
Unix versions require local compilation.

okay, that's enough niceness for one article.

